    // Obfuscating attacks using encodings
    "In this section, we'll show you how you can take advantage of the standard decoding performed by websites to evade input filters and inject harmful payloads for a variety of attacks, such as XSS and SQL injection." => 'Bagian ini menjelaskan cara memanfaatkan mekanisme dekode standar di situs web untuk melewati filter masukan pada serangan seperti XSS dan SQL injection.',
    'Context-specific decoding' => 'Dekode sesuai konteks',
    'Both clients and servers use a variety of different encodings to pass data between systems. When they want to actually use the data, this often means they have to decode it first. The exact sequence of decoding steps that are performed depends on the context in which the data appears. For example, a query parameter is typically URL decoded server-side, while the text content of an HTML element may be HTML decoded client-side.' => 'Klien maupun server saling mengirim data menggunakan berbagai encoding lalu mendekodenya sebelum dipakai. Jenis dekode bergantung pada konteksnya: parameter kueri mengalami URL decode di server, sedangkan konten elemen HTML mengalami HTML decode di peramban.',
    'When constructing an attack, you should think about where exactly your payload is being injected. If you can infer how your input is being decoded based on this context, you can potentially identify alternative ways to represent the same payload.' => 'Dengan mengenali di konteks mana masukan disuntikkan dan urutan dekodenya, Anda dapat menuliskan payload yang sama dalam format alternatif.',
    'Decoding discrepancies' => 'Ketidaksesuaian proses dekode',
    'Injection attacks often involve injecting payloads that use recognizable patterns, such as HTML tags, JavaScript functions, or SQL statements. As the inputs for these payloads are almost never expected to contain user-supplied code or markup, websites often implement defences that block requests containing these suspicious patterns.' => 'Filter keamanan umumnya mencari pola berbahaya seperti tag HTML, fungsi JavaScript, atau kata kunci SQL lalu memblokirnya.',
    "However, these kinds of input filters also need to decode the input in order to check whether it's safe or not. From a security perspective, it's vital that the decoding performed when checking the input is the same as the decoding performed by the back-end server or browser when it eventually uses the data. Any discrepancy can enable an attacker to sneak harmful payloads past the filter by applying different encodings that will automatically be removed later." => 'Agar efektif, filter harus mendekode masukan persis seperti cara backend atau peramban mendekodenya. Perbedaan sekecil apa pun memungkinkan payload terselundupkan melewati pemeriksaan filter.',
    'Obfuscation via URL encoding' => 'Penyamaran melalui URL encoding',
